id: pm-github-znig
title: Let reusable workflows carry their own release version
description: Resolve reusable sync and closeout package versions at runtime from the release tag on documented job.workflow_sha. Public git ls-remote handles lightweight and peeled annotated tags without new credentials. Exact legacy-input fallback is deprecated and only allowed when no release tag matches; otherwise fail closed or warn and use the tag version. Restore release.yml token behavior without stamping or GitHub App setup. Retain daily Dependabot SHA updates and caller templates without version input. No caller repins or release dispatch.
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-16T12:47:09.319Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-16T15:28:48.086Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Real workflow bash contracts prove tag and peeled-tag matching, exact installs, no-match legacy fallback, fail-closed absent fallback, mismatch warnings and injection safety; npm and Bun release checks pass at unchanged thresholds; release stamping and app minting are removed."
comments[11]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-16T12:47:21.478Z",codex-agent,"Design: release preparation stamps both reusable workflow input defaults and literal PM_GITHUB_VERSION job values from the prepared package version, before release checks and the metadata commit. The job always installs and verifies that literal exact version; REQUESTED_PM_GITHUB_VERSION carries the deprecated input only for a non-fatal mismatch warning. Both workflow paths join release commit and merged-state diff scopes. Contract tests execute real release/validation/install shell blocks with isolated files and command receipts. Caller docs use daily github-actions updates grouped as pm-toolchain, the existing auto-merge exemption for calendar-version major changes; commit prefix and labels do not authorize merging."
  "2026-10-16T12:52:56.211Z",codex-agent,"Found an operational requirement: stamping .github/workflows files requires Workflows write authorization, which GITHUB_TOKEN cannot grant. Added a SHA-pinned GitHub App token step with explicit repository permissions, checkout/release-PR authentication, and a missing-configuration refusal before version preparation. Tokens are minted and revoked automatically. Follow-up pm-github-ygye tracks the one-time app installation and configuration; no credential or release dispatch was changed. Sources: https://docs.github.com/en/rest/repos/contents#create-or-update-file-contents and https://docs.github.com/en/actions/tutorials/authenticate-with-github_token#granting-additional-permissions ."
  "2026-10-16T12:54:28.432Z",codex-agent,"Behavioural revert proofs using node --test --test-reporter=tap test/self-versioned-workflows.test.ts, keeping all tests unchanged and restoring each implementation mutation immediately: remove only release stamping block => 15 pass / 4 fail; restore only caller-controlled install binding => 9 pass / 10 fail; remove only mismatch warning => 13 pass / 6 fail; restore only deprecated caller-template input => 17 pass / 2 fail; remove only workflow paths from release commit staging => 17 pass / 2 fail. Each run has 19 tests and zero skip/cancel/todo. Restored implementation passes 19/19, also verified through pm test --run --progress. Dedicated app setup remains tracked by pm-github-ygye; no release or fleet-repin actions performed."
  "2026-10-16T13:27:48.638Z",codex-agent,"First isolated-identity npm release gate reached 721 tests: 720 passed, one attestation contract failed, with zero skip/cancel/todo. The pinned attestation scanner treated TypeScript template literals in the new release heredoc as shell command substitutions and reported false publish paths. Replaced those template literals with equivalent string concatenation; release behavior and thresholds are unchanged. Running the direct verifier and release contracts before repeating the full gates."
  "2026-10-16T13:29:07.696Z",codex-agent,"Corrected source: direct attestation verifier passes and node --test test/self-versioned-workflows.test.ts test/release-workflow.test.ts test/verify-release-publish-attestation.test.ts passes 36/36 with zero fail/skip/cancel/todo. Explicit empty legacy input now also warns. Repeated all five implementation-only revert proofs with unchanged current tests: remove stamping => 15 pass / 4 fail; revert install binding => 9 pass / 10 fail; remove warning => 11 pass / 8 fail; restore template input => 17 pass / 2 fail; omit workflows from release staging => 17 pass / 2 fail. Each has 19 tests and zero skip/cancel/todo. All mutations restored; the full npm and Bun gates will run again at unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-10-16T14:21:44.001Z",codex-agent,"Final gates passed on the restored implementation at unchanged thresholds: npm run release:check under isolated HOME with global/system Git configuration disabled, and bun run release:check. Each reports 721/721 tests, zero failures, skips, cancellations or TODOs; both require exact 100/100/100/100 coverage across 13 authored modules. Typecheck, docstrings, lint, zero-duplication, privacy, production audit (zero vulnerabilities), dry-run packing, changelog and publish-attestation checks passed. Focused release contracts passed 36/36; linked pm test passed 19/19. The heredoc scanner false positive is avoided with string concatenation. No release dispatched or other fleet repository edited. Release-app configuration and scheduled acceptance remain open in pm-github-ygye; this feature remains unclosed with its claim released."
  "2026-10-16T14:27:44.968Z",codex-agent,"Round 1: replace release stamping and release-app minting with runtime release-tag lookup. Verified official GitHub contexts reference: job.workflow_sha is the commit of the workflow defining the current job, including reusable workflows; github.job_workflow_sha is not a documented context (job_workflow_sha is an OIDC claim). Use job.workflow_sha through step env and public git ls-remote, with peeled annotated tags, exact version validation, legacy-input fallback only on no matching tag, and fail-closed lookup errors. No additional credentials or permissions. origin/main is already an ancestor of this branch; no merge needed."
  "2026-10-16T14:30:42.654Z",codex-agent,"Runtime contracts pass 36/36 (also via pm test --run --progress), executing extracted resolver and install scripts through bash with an injected git ls-remote seam. Covers lightweight/peeled tags, reverse advertisement order, unrelated/malformed tags, exact suffixes, absent tags with/without fallback, mismatch warnings, malicious inputs, lookup failures, missing identity, ambiguous releases and installed-version mismatch. Behavioral revert proof with tests unchanged: restoring only the prior embedded-version selection in sync fails its resolver scenarios; separately restoring only closeout selection fails its scenarios. Restoring the prior release stamping/app implementation fails the release contract. All implementations restored and contracts pass again. release.yml is byte-identical to origin/main. Documentation: https://docs.github.com/en/actions/reference/workflows-and-actions/contexts#job-context ."
  "2026-10-16T14:32:24.094Z",codex-agent,"Exact behavioral revert counts: sync selection reverted alone => 0/16 pass and 16 fail; closeout selection reverted alone => 0/16 pass and 16 fail; prior release implementation restored alone => 0/1 pass and 1 fail. Each run has zero skipped, canceled or TODO tests. Restored implementation passes 36/36. A read-only live run of the actual resolver against the released main commit resolves PM_GITHUB_VERSION=2026.10.16 from public tags without credentials."
  "2026-10-16T15:03:50.189Z",codex-agent,"Round 1 npm gate passed: env HOME=$(mktemp -d) GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1 npm run release:check. Full suite 738/738, zero failures/skips/cancellations/TODOs; exact 100/100/100/100 coverage across 13 authored modules; docstrings, lint, zero duplication, privacy, production audit (zero vulnerabilities), pack dry run, changelog check and publish-attestation verification all passed. Re-fetched origin: main is unchanged and remains an ancestor. Starting bun run release:check at unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-10-16T15:28:47.265Z",codex-agent,"Round 1 complete locally: bun run release:check also passes 738/738 with zero failures/skips/cancellations/TODOs and exact 100/100/100/100 coverage across 13 authored modules. Both npm and Bun gates pass unchanged thresholds, including docstrings, lint, zero duplication, privacy, production audit (zero vulnerabilities), pack dry run, changelog check and attestation verification. Resolver contracts pass 36/36 and implementation-only revert proofs are recorded above. Runtime uses documented job.workflow_sha and public peeled-tag lookup, without new credentials or permissions; release.yml matches origin/main. pm-github-ygye has the supersession comment and stays open for orchestrator cancellation. No hosted consumer workflow or release dispatched. Finalize tracker/changelog, commit and push PR 139, then poll its GitHub checks every 60 seconds for at most 30 minutes; final hosted check results will be reported in the handoff. No new PM CLI defects identified."
